  "question": {
    "html": "<p>The diagram shows three energy levels of an atom. When an electron transitions from a higher energy level to a lower one, a photon is emitted. The wavelengths of the photons emitted during the transitions <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"n=3\"></span> to <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"n=2\"></span> and <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"n=2\"></span> to <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"n=1\"></span> are <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\lambda_{32}\"></span> and <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\lambda_{21}\"></span>, respectively.</p>\n<p><figure data-asset-id=\"fig_01\"><img alt=\"Source question diagram 1\" src=\"asset:fig_01\"/></figure></p>\n<p>Which expression gives the wavelength <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\lambda_{31}\"></span> of the photon emitted during the transition from <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"n=3\"></span> to <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"n=1\"></span>?</p><ol class=\"mcq-options\"><li data-label=\"A\"><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\lambda_{31} = \\lambda_{32} + \\lambda_{21}\"></span></p></li><li data-label=\"B\"><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\lambda_{31} = \\frac{\\lambda_{32} + \\lambda_{21}}{\\lambda_{32} \\lambda_{21}}\"></span></p></li><li data-label=\"C\"><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\lambda_{31} = \\frac{\\lambda_{32} \\lambda_{21}}{\\lambda_{32} + \\lambda_{21}}\"></span></p></li><li data-label=\"D\"><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\lambda_{31} = \\sqrt{\\lambda_{32} \\lambda_{21}}\"></span></p></li></ol>"
  },
